在流动厕所那边，他们在采访一位带着三个孩子的无家可归单身母亲。

1406
01:02:13.720 --> 01:02:14.120
What?
什么？

1407
01:02:14.300 --> 01:02:14.800
Who cares?
谁在乎？

1408
01:02:18.360 --> 01:02:19.020
Is that your ride?
那是来接你的车吗？

1409
01:02:20.600 --> 01:02:21.880
What is going on?
这到底是怎么回事？

1410
01:02:27.520 --> 01:02:29.240
What is happening?
发生什么事了？

1411
01:02:29.720 --> 01:02:31.480
I think we can keep that one.
我觉得我们可以保留那段。

1412
01:02:31.680 --> 01:02:32.420
What is happening?
发生什么事了？

1413
01:02:32.600 --> 01:02:34.460
Is that a bank robbery?
那是抢劫银行吗？

1414
01:02:34.740 --> 01:02:35.220
What just happened?
刚刚发生了什么？

1415
01:02:35.220 --> 01:02:35.860
It was crazy.
太疯狂了。

1416
01:02:37.580 --> 01:02:40.930
Are you all allowed?
你们都被允许吗？

1417
01:02:41.330 --> 01:02:41.470
Yes.
是的。

1418
01:02:41.790 --> 01:02:42.070
Yes.
是的。

1419
01:02:42.310 --> 01:02:42.550
Yeah.
是啊。

1420
01:02:42.870 --> 01:02:46.150
Well, I asked Jessica about this and here's what she had to say.
好吧，我问过杰西卡这件事，以下是她的说法。

1421
01:02:47.410 --> 01:02:55.250
Now, apparently there was a drag race happening during the scene when we were standing online.
现在，显然当我们排队时，那个场景正在发生一场飙车。

1422
01:02:55.250 --> 01:03:04.170
I don't have a memory of that, but I do remember that everyone on the line, all the background
我不记得那个了，但我确实记得排队的每个人，所有的背景

1423
01:03:04.170 --> 01:03:11.410
actors were so lovely and just a fun hang, you know, and that isn't always the case, but
演员都非常可爱，在一起玩得很开心，你知道，情况并不总是这样，但

1424
01:03:11.410 --> 01:03:13.070
everyone was so excited to be there.
每个人都很高兴能来到这里。

1425
01:03:13.190 --> 01:03:17.750
I think there was, you know, everyone was sort of a fan of the office and everyone was
我想，你知道的，每个人都算是《办公室》的粉丝，每个人都

1426
01:03:17.750 --> 01:03:20.470
really bringing like a backstory to their characters.
真的给他们的角色带来了一个背景故事。

1427
01:03:20.470 --> 01:03:21.550
So that was really fun.
所以这真的很有趣。

1428
01:03:22.210 --> 01:03:27.410
You know, some of my favorite things to shoot are like situations like this where you're in
你知道，我最喜欢拍摄的一些事情就是像这样的情况，你处于

1429
01:03:27.410 --> 01:03:34.170
this like big line or big group of people for multiple scenes because you really do kind
这个大队伍或一大群人中拍好几个场景，因为你真的

1430
01:03:34.170 --> 01:03:38.990
of end up making up your own stories in the background and they become some of the most
最终会在背景中编造你自己的故事，而这些成了最

1431
01:03:38.990 --> 01:03:39.870
fun shoot days.
有趣的拍摄日。

1432
01:03:40.310 --> 01:03:40.490
Yeah.
是啊。

1433
01:03:40.690 --> 01:03:43.030
There's a guy with a cowboy hat in the background.
背景里有个戴牛仔帽的家伙。

1434
01:03:43.410 --> 01:03:43.790
Yes.
对。

1435
01:03:43.830 --> 01:03:44.710
I kept watching him.
我一直在看他。

1436
01:03:44.870 --> 01:03:46.590
He clearly had a story for himself.
他显然为自己编了一段故事。

1437
01:03:46.590 --> 01:03:51.530
I should point out that our guest star who played the veteran was Nico Evers Swindle.
我应该指出，饰演退伍军人的客串明星是尼科·埃弗斯-斯温德尔。

1438
01:03:51.670 --> 01:03:54.650
He has been on Veep, American Horror Story and Grimm.
他曾出演过《副总统》、《美国恐怖故事》和《格林》。

1439
01:03:54.790 --> 01:03:57.930
He also played Prince William in the movie William and Kate.
他还曾在电影《威廉与凯特》中饰演威廉王子。

1440
01:03:58.590 --> 01:03:59.050
Wow.
哇。

1441
01:03:59.310 --> 01:03:59.590
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1442
01:04:00.050 --> 01:04:02.670
And everyone, Jessica is so amazing and funny.
而且大家，杰西卡是如此出色和幽默。

1443
01:04:02.790 --> 01:04:05.470
We're going to have more audio clips to share with you next week.
我们下周还会有更多音频剪辑与大家分享。

1444
01:04:05.470 --> 01:04:10.470
And definitely check out her podcast with June Diane Raphael called The Deep Dive.
一定要去听听她和琼·黛安·拉斐尔主持的播客，叫做《深入探讨》。

1445
01:04:10.630 --> 01:04:14.750
And you also have to listen to her audio book with Casey Wilson.
你还得听她和凯西·威尔逊合作的有声书。

1446
01:04:15.030 --> 01:04:17.630
It is called The Art of Small Talk.
它叫做《闲聊的艺术》。

1447
01:04:17.930 --> 01:04:19.070
It's on Audible.
它在Audible上。

1448
01:04:19.330 --> 01:04:20.490
It is so funny.
太搞笑了。

1449
01:04:20.690 --> 01:04:22.950
The two of them are so hilarious.
他们两个太滑稽了。

1450
01:04:23.310 --> 01:04:28.270
They're going to give you all the advice you need to go to any event with some great small
他们会给你提供你需要的所有建议，让你带着精彩的闲聊去参加任何活动

1451
01:04:28.270 --> 01:04:28.530
talk.
说话。

1452
01:04:28.670 --> 01:04:33.570
I feel like my trick of walking up to people laughing could be in this book.
我觉得我那种走近别人并大笑的把戏也可以写进这本书里。

1453
01:04:33.710 --> 01:04:33.950
Okay.
好的。

1454
01:04:33.950 --> 01:04:37.550
That's just a preview of some of their advice.
那只是他们一些建议的预览。

1455
01:04:38.070 --> 01:04:39.790
I think that would qualify.
我觉得那完全符合资格。

1456
01:04:39.970 --> 01:04:41.030
They would like it.
他们会喜欢的。

1457
01:04:41.550 --> 01:04:45.450
Well, Andy is going to decide if the judges want a feel-good moment, he's going to give
好吧，安迪打算由他来决定评委们是否想要一个温馨感人的时刻，他要给

1458
01:04:45.450 --> 01:04:46.510
them a feel-good moment.
他们一个温馨感人的时刻。

1459
01:04:46.570 --> 01:04:48.610
He says, save my place in line.
他说，帮我占着队里的位子。

1460
01:04:48.750 --> 01:04:49.650
And he takes off.
然后他跑开了。

1461
01:04:49.770 --> 01:04:50.050
Yeah.
对。

1462
01:04:50.430 --> 01:04:51.810
What's Andy got up his sleeve?
安迪葫芦里卖的什么药？

1463
01:04:52.090 --> 01:04:53.950
Oh, something good.
哦，绝对是好东西。

1464
01:04:54.110 --> 01:04:54.390
Oh.
哦。

1465
01:04:55.170 --> 01:04:56.970
We're over at Caffeine Corner now.
我们现在来到了咖啡角。

1466
01:04:57.110 --> 01:04:58.730
And I'll be damned if they don't have donuts.
真没想到他们竟然有甜甜圈。

1467
01:04:59.510 --> 01:05:00.310
Caffeine Corner.
咖啡角。

1468
01:05:00.430 --> 01:05:01.230
So many donuts.
有好多甜甜圈。

1469
01:05:01.650 --> 01:05:02.890
They never had donuts.
他们以前从没供应过甜甜圈。

1470
01:05:03.550 --> 01:05:06.970
I remember being super excited to go over there.
我记得当时去那边时兴奋极了。

1471
01:05:06.970 --> 01:05:08.250
And I did sneak one.
我还偷吃了一个。

1472
01:05:08.450 --> 01:05:09.570
They let me have one.
他们让我吃了一个。

1473
01:05:09.670 --> 01:05:12.850
Well, that's where we were doing all of our interviews for The Look Back.
哦，那是我们为《回看》做所有采访的地方。

1474
01:05:13.110 --> 01:05:13.290
Yeah.
是啊。

1475
01:05:13.810 --> 01:05:14.090
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1476
01:05:14.690 --> 01:05:17.210
Daryl's going to buy some to give some of the warehouse guys.
达里尔要买一些送给仓库的伙计们。

1477
01:05:17.510 --> 01:05:19.850
He felt bad, I guess, because he didn't say goodbye to them.
我猜他觉得挺内疚的，因为他没跟他们道别。

1478
01:05:19.850 --> 01:05:22.750
And Pam asked him, how's it going at Athlead?
帕姆问他，在“アスリード”那边怎么样？

1479
01:05:23.350 --> 01:05:24.590
Daryl couldn't be happier.
达里尔高兴极了。

1480
01:05:24.730 --> 01:05:25.610
He's so stoked.
他兴奋惨了。

1481
01:05:25.750 --> 01:05:27.990
He's going to meet all of his sports heroes.
他能见到他所有的体育偶像。

1482
01:05:28.190 --> 01:05:29.710
He'll go to 32 different cities.
他要去32个不同的城市。

1483
01:05:29.790 --> 01:05:33.110
He can't believe that Jim is happier at Dunder Mifflin.
他简直不敢相信吉姆在邓德米弗林会更开心。

1484
01:05:33.490 --> 01:05:33.770
Yeah.
对。

1485
01:05:34.230 --> 01:05:38.210
He says he's not having any second thoughts about leaving Athlead.
他说他离开“アスリード”后一点也没有后悔。

1486
01:05:38.370 --> 01:05:39.870
And Pam is like, nope.
然后帕姆的反应是，没有。

1487
01:05:40.130 --> 01:05:41.650
I mean, he seems happy.
我是说，他看起来很开心。

1488
01:05:41.850 --> 01:05:42.850
He seems happy.
他看起来很开心。

1489
01:05:42.850 --> 01:05:46.430
He's just going to try to recreate Office Olympics, pretty much.
他基本上就是打算重现办公室奥运会。

1490
01:05:46.430 --> 01:05:47.910
Maybe a call for help.
也许是在呼救吧。

1491
01:05:48.390 --> 01:05:49.650
We're in the warehouse.
我们在仓库里。

1492
01:05:50.250 --> 01:05:54.470
And there is a coffee obstacle course set up.
这里设置了一个咖啡障碍赛。

1493
01:05:54.710 --> 01:05:56.610
Yeah, you have two cups of hot coffee.
对，你要端两杯热咖啡。

1494
01:05:56.690 --> 01:05:57.990
Your boss needs his coffee.
你老板需要他的咖啡。

1495
01:05:58.270 --> 01:05:59.130
Here's the thing.
问题是这样的。

1496
01:05:59.270 --> 01:06:00.410
It's super piping hot.
咖啡烫得冒烟。

1497
01:06:00.930 --> 01:06:06.150
You got to step over three different sizes of, like, stacks of paper.
你得跨过三种不同高度的纸堆。

1498
01:06:06.150 --> 01:06:10.610
And then you go through this chair obstacle spinny thing.
然后你要穿过那个旋转椅子的障碍。

1499
01:06:10.830 --> 01:06:12.790
Yeah, the chairs are upside down.
对，椅子是倒过来的。

1500
01:06:12.950 --> 01:06:13.990
The wheels are spinning.
轮子还在转。

1501
01:06:14.390 --> 01:06:18.110
This obstacle course was originally scripted to be outside.
这个障碍赛原本剧本设定是在室外。

1502
01:06:18.370 --> 01:06:20.730
But Dave Rogers moved it into the warehouse.
但戴夫·罗杰斯把它搬到了仓库里。

1503
01:06:20.790 --> 01:06:22.870
He said he moved it for two reasons.
他说他搬到里面有两个原因。

1504
01:06:23.430 --> 01:06:33.890
One, because he thought it would be easier for Aaron to spot Daryl at the end if they were in the warehouse than if they were outside in the alley.
第一，他觉得如果在仓库里，阿伦会比在室外的巷子里更容易在终点看到达里尔。

1505
01:06:33.890 --> 01:06:42.090
But also, he said whenever we did a lot of scenes outside, we would all get hot and grouchy.
但同时他还说，每当我们拍很多室外戏时，大家都会变得又热又暴躁。

1506
01:06:42.830 --> 01:06:46.610
And so he was like, let's move it inside, folks.
所以他就说，伙计们，我们把它搬到室内吧。

1507
01:06:47.050 --> 01:06:47.530
Save myself.
顺便拯救一下我自己。

1508
01:06:47.810 --> 01:06:48.110
Exactly.
没错。

1509
01:06:48.630 --> 01:06:49.650
Some grouchy folks.
一群暴躁的家伙。

1510
01:06:50.450 --> 01:06:52.990
Phyllis is up first on the obstacle course.
菲莉丝第一个上场挑战障碍赛。

1511
01:06:53.410 --> 01:06:55.730
And she's moving too slowly.
而且她动得太慢了。

1512
01:06:56.330 --> 01:06:57.650
Dwight can't take it.
德怀特可看不下去了。

1513
01:06:57.910 --> 01:07:00.350
He, like, grabs the coffee from her, starts running through it.
他一把抢过她的咖啡，开始冲过障碍。

1514
01:07:00.350 --> 01:07:01.650
He's spilling coffee on himself.
咖啡都洒到他自己身上了。

1515
01:07:01.650 --> 01:07:02.810
It's, like, burning him.
感觉就像在烫伤他一样。

1516
01:07:02.810 --> 01:07:03.590
But you know what?
但你知道吗？

1517
01:07:03.590 --> 01:07:07.170
He's going to get that coffee to his boss, which is himself.
他要把那杯咖啡送到他的老板手里，也就是他自己。

1518
01:07:07.910 --> 01:07:13.510
I would like to award myself a Razzie for my performance in this scene.
我想为我在这场戏里的表现给自己颁发一个金酸莓奖。

1519
01:07:13.710 --> 01:07:14.310
Oh, my God.
哦，天呐。

1520
01:07:14.310 --> 01:07:16.030
I could barely watch it.
我简直没眼看。

1521
01:07:16.470 --> 01:07:21.850
Could I be telegraphing or showing or indicating anymore?
我还能把表演痕迹表现得、显露得、暗示得更明显一点吗？

1522
01:07:22.830 --> 01:07:26.570
Everyone, if you want to be an actor, don't do what I'm doing in this scene.
各位，如果你们想当演员，千万别学我在这场戏里的演法。

1523
01:07:26.690 --> 01:07:26.830
Stop it.
够了。

1524
01:07:27.030 --> 01:07:27.750
I'm serious.
我是认真的。

1525
01:07:28.110 --> 01:07:32.170
Like, everything about me, it's like, does anyone have eyes on me?
就好像我全身都在说，有没有人在注意我？

1526
01:07:32.170 --> 01:07:40.690
Like, how is Jim not noticing that I've turned into a complete sad sack and I'm just standing there like a big, wet blanket?
吉姆怎么会没注意到我已经变成了一个彻底的废柴，就那么像个扫兴的讨厌鬼一样站在那儿？

1527
01:07:41.050 --> 01:07:43.110
I mean, how about some subtlety, Jenna?
我是说，讲点含蓄好吗，珍娜？

1528
01:07:43.750 --> 01:07:48.430
When Jenna says a Razzie award, she's talking about a thing called the Golden Raspberry Awards.
珍娜说的金酸莓奖，是颁给一种叫金酸莓奖的东西。

1529
01:07:48.670 --> 01:07:52.890
It's a parody and it's an award show honoring the worst in cinematic failures.
这是一个讽刺性的奖项，专门表彰电影界最烂的失败之作。

1530
01:07:52.890 --> 01:07:53.710
Yes.
没错。

1531
01:07:54.030 --> 01:07:59.110
They don't even cover television, but I think they should make an exception for me in this scene.
它们甚至不涵盖电视节目，但我觉得它们应该为我在这场戏里的表现破个例。

1532
01:07:59.190 --> 01:07:59.240
Stop it.
住手。

1533
01:07:59.430 --> 01:08:00.190
I disagree.
我不同意。

1534
01:08:00.670 --> 01:08:00.950
Ugh.
呃。

1535
01:08:01.270 --> 01:08:13.270
Well, anyway, as if you couldn't tell, Pam is now very preoccupied with this idea that Daryl has planted in her head that maybe Jim is not actually as happy as he seeMs.
总之，正如你所见，潘现在满脑子都在琢磨达里尔塞给她脑子里的那个想法，也许吉姆其实并不像他看起来那么快乐。

1536
01:08:13.270 --> 01:08:19.130
Yeah, Jim is going to present Dwight with a crown that he's made out of, like, tinfoil and cardboard.
对，吉姆准备把一顶他用锡纸和纸板做的王冠颁给德怀特。

1537
01:08:19.510 --> 01:08:20.870
Everyone applauds but Pam.
所有人都鼓掌了，除了潘。

1538
01:08:21.010 --> 01:08:22.410
In fact, she runs outside.
事实上，她跑到了外面。

1539
01:08:22.710 --> 01:08:23.790
Very dramatically.
非常戏剧化地。

1540
01:08:24.110 --> 01:08:25.030
Runs away.
跑走了。

1541
01:08:26.250 --> 01:08:27.750
Overly dramatic, Pam.
太戏剧化了，潘。

1542
01:08:28.430 --> 01:08:32.470
Dave said that Rain improvised a line at the end of this scene.
戴夫说雷恩在这场戏的结尾即兴发挥了一句台词。

1543
01:08:32.850 --> 01:08:35.990
Originally, it was going to end with Pam running out.
原本的结局应该是潘跑出去。

1544
01:08:36.550 --> 01:08:39.510
But Rain improvised this line and I loved it so much.
但雷恩即兴加了这句台词，我太喜欢了。

1545
01:08:39.770 --> 01:08:44.450
He says, from now on, anyone who needs to speak to me has got to go through me firSt.
他说，从今以后，任何需要跟我讲话的人都必须先通过我这一关。

1546
01:08:44.870 --> 01:08:46.750
I thought it was really funny.
我觉得这真的很有趣。

1547
01:08:48.010 --> 01:08:50.090
Rain knew his character so well.
雷恩太了解他的角色了。

1548
01:08:50.250 --> 01:08:50.690
So well.
太了解了。

1549
01:08:50.990 --> 01:08:53.290
Well, Jim is going to catch up to Pam outside.
接着，吉姆在外面追上了潘。

1550
01:08:53.290 --> 01:08:55.410
They're in that little alley by the warehouse.
他们就在仓库旁边的那个小巷子里。

1551
01:08:55.890 --> 01:08:56.970
And she's worried.
而且她很担心。

1552
01:08:57.110 --> 01:08:58.010
Jim's like, are you okay?
吉姆就问，你还好吗？

1553
01:08:58.010 --> 01:08:59.530
And she says, today was fun.
她说，今天挺开心的。

1554
01:08:59.610 --> 01:09:00.710
But what about a year from now?
但一年后呢？

1555
01:09:00.810 --> 01:09:02.310
What about five years from now?
五年后呢？

1556
01:09:02.310 --> 01:09:07.770
You know, she's worried that she's not enough for him and that he's going to resent her.
你知道的，她担心自己配不上他，担心他会怨恨她。

1557
01:09:08.070 --> 01:09:09.430
I need to pick up my mug.
我得去拿我的马克杯。

1558
01:09:09.590 --> 01:09:09.930
Okay.
好的。

1559
01:09:10.210 --> 01:09:11.070
Here it comes.
